IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa12-logic`
IMPORT `coa12-ch5-concerns`

-- coa12-tests-ch5.l4: tests for coa12-ch5-concerns.l4 (ss 527-531). Expected values are decided from the text before the run and
-- written beside each assertion. Argument order is the GIVEN order of each function.

-- ---- s 531(1): quoted company for this Chapter (the s 385 answer passes through)
#ASSERT `s 531(1) the company is a quoted company for the purposes of this Chapter` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 531(1) the company is a quoted company for the purposes of this Chapter` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 531(1) the company is a quoted company for the purposes of this Chapter` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 527(1): the members' power (quoted company, a matter about the audit or about an auditor ceasing to hold office, to be raised at the next accounts meeting)
#ASSERT `s 527(1) the members may require the company to publish the statement on a website` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 527(1) the members may require the company to publish the statement on a website` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 527(1) the members may require the company to publish the statement on a website` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 527(1) the members may require the company to publish the statement on a website` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a company that is not quoted: the power is for "the members of a quoted company"; not covered
#ASSERT `s 527(1) the members may require the company to publish the statement on a website` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 527(1) the members may require the company to publish the statement on a website` NOTHING TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 527(2): the thresholds: (a) 5% of the voting rights; (b) at least 100 members with an average of at least 100 pounds paid up
#ASSERT `s 527(2) the company is required to publish the statement on a website` 0.05 0 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 527(2) the company is required to publish the statement on a website` 0.0499 0 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 527(2) the company is required to publish the statement on a website` 0.01 100 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 527(2) the company is required to publish the statement on a website` 0.01 99 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 527(2) the company is required to publish the statement on a website` 0.01 100 99.99 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 527(2) the company is required to publish the statement on a website` 0 200 150 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 527(2) the company is required to publish the statement on a website` 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a) alone suffices even where (b) is far short
#ASSERT `s 527(2) the company is required to publish the statement on a website` 0.2 3 10 EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 527(3): "relevant right to vote"
#ASSERT `s 527(3) the right is a relevant right to vote` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 527(3) the right is a relevant right to vote` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 527(4): the request. The meeting is on 15 March 2026; "at least one week before" is on or before 8 March.
#ASSERT `s 527(4) the request is a valid request` `hard copy form` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (Date 8 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 527(4) the request is a valid request` `electronic form` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (Date 8 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 527(4) the request is a valid request` `electronic form` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (Date 9 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 527(4) the request is a valid request` `electronic form` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 527(4) the request is a valid request` `electronic form` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 527(4) the request is a valid request` `electronic form` TRUE NOTHING (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 527(4) the request is a valid request` `electronic form` FALSE NOTHING (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 527(5), (6): abuse of the rights; costs
#ASSERT `s 527(5) the quoted company is required to place the statement on a website` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 527(5) the quoted company is required to place the statement on a website` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 527(6) the court may order the members requesting website publication to pay the company's costs on the application` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 527(6) the court may order the members requesting website publication to pay the company's costs on the application` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 528: website availability
#ASSERT `s 528(2) the website meets the requirement` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 528(2) the website meets the requirement` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 528(2) the website meets the requirement` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 528(3) the access to the information meets the requirement` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 528(3) the access to the information meets the requirement` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4)(a): three working days: 0 to 3 in time, 4 not
#ASSERT `s 528(4)(a) the statement was made available within three working days of the company being required to publish it` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 528(4)(a) the statement was made available within three working days of the company being required to publish it` 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 528(4)(a) the statement was made available within three working days of the company being required to publish it` 4 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 528(4)(a) the statement was made available within three working days of the company being required to publish it` (-1) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 528(4)(b) the statement was kept available until after the meeting to which it relates` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 528(4)(b) the statement was kept available until after the meeting to which it relates` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 528(5) the failure to make the information available throughout the period is disregarded` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 528(5) the failure to make the information available throughout the period is disregarded` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 528(5) the failure to make the information available throughout the period is disregarded` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 529: the company's supplementary duties
#ASSERT `s 529(1) the quoted company must draw attention in the notice of the accounts meeting` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 529(1) the quoted company must draw attention in the notice of the accounts meeting` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 529(1) the quoted company must draw attention in the notice of the accounts meeting` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 529(1) the notice draws attention to what the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 529(1) the notice draws attention to what the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 529(1) the notice draws attention to what the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 529(2) the company may require the members requesting website publication to pay its expenses` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 529(2) the company may require the members requesting website publication to pay its expenses` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 529(3) the company must forward the statement to the company's auditor` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 529(3) the company must forward the statement to the company's auditor` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3): not later than the time it is made available (1 March 2026, 10 o'clock)
#ASSERT `s 529(3) the statement was forwarded to the auditor not later than the time it was made available on the website` (JUST (`s 529(3) time` OF (Date 1 3 2026), 10)) (`s 529(3) time` OF (Date 1 3 2026), 10) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 529(3) the statement was forwarded to the auditor not later than the time it was made available on the website` (JUST (`s 529(3) time` OF (Date 1 3 2026), 9.5)) (`s 529(3) time` OF (Date 1 3 2026), 10) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 529(3) the statement was forwarded to the auditor not later than the time it was made available on the website` (JUST (`s 529(3) time` OF (Date 1 3 2026), 10.5)) (`s 529(3) time` OF (Date 1 3 2026), 10) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 529(3) the statement was forwarded to the auditor not later than the time it was made available on the website` (JUST (`s 529(3) time` OF (Date 28 2 2026), 23)) (`s 529(3) time` OF (Date 1 3 2026), 10) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 529(3) the statement was forwarded to the auditor not later than the time it was made available on the website` (JUST (`s 529(3) time` OF (Date 2 3 2026), 0)) (`s 529(3) time` OF (Date 1 3 2026), 10) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 529(3) the statement was forwarded to the auditor not later than the time it was made available on the website` NOTHING (`s 529(3) time` OF (Date 1 3 2026), 10) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 529(4) the business which may be dealt with at the accounts meeting includes the statement` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 529(4) the business which may be dealt with at the accounts meeting includes the statement` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 530: the offence (default under s 528 or s 529; officer in default, s 1121)
#ASSERT `s 530(1) the officer of the company commits an offence` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530(1) the officer of the company commits an offence` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 530(1) the officer of the company commits an offence` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 530(1) the officer of the company commits an offence` TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 530(1) the officer of the company commits an offence` FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): on indictment a fine; on summary conviction a fine up to the statutory maximum
#ASSERT `s 530(2) the penalty for an offence under this section` `on conviction on indictment` EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 530(2) the penalty for an offence under this section` `on summary conviction` EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 530(2) the penalty for an offence under this section` `on summary conviction in Scotland` EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, FALSE)

-- ---- the helper of coa12-logic that counts a period from a day (both ends in): within 14 days after 1 March 2026 is 1 March to 15 March; n = 27 is the period of 28 days beginning with the day
#ASSERT `coa12 the act was done within the number of days after the day` (JUST (Date 1 3 2026)) (Date 1 3 2026) 14 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `coa12 the act was done within the number of days after the day` (JUST (Date 15 3 2026)) (Date 1 3 2026) 14 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `coa12 the act was done within the number of days after the day` (JUST (Date 16 3 2026)) (Date 1 3 2026) 14 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `coa12 the act was done within the number of days after the day` (JUST (Date 28 2 2026)) (Date 1 3 2026) 14 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `coa12 the act was done within the number of days after the day` (JUST (Date 28 3 2026)) (Date 1 3 2026) 27 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `coa12 the act was done within the number of days after the day` (JUST (Date 29 3 2026)) (Date 1 3 2026) 27 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `coa12 the act was done within the number of days after the day` NOTHING (Date 1 3 2026) 14 EQUALS FALSE

-- ---- the deontic forms run (traces are read, not asserted: see NOTES.md). The clock of s 528(4)(a) counts working days.
#TRACE `s 528(4)(a) the company's duty to make the statement available on a website` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "make the statement available on a website within three working days of being required to publish it" AT 3
#TRACE `s 528(4)(a) the company's duty to make the statement available on a website` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 4
#TRACE `s 529(3) the company's duty to forward the statement to the auditor` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `Action of a party` OF Company, Auditor, "forward the statement to the company's auditor" AT 0
